<title>USA: ASHLAND IN NIGERIA TALKS WITH TOTAL.</title>
<headline>ASHLAND IN NIGERIA TALKS WITH TOTAL.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ashland Inc said it is in talks with France's Total SA over a production block whose license was revoked by Nigeria's government earlier this year.</p>
<p>&quot;Ashland has met with Nigeria's Honourable Minister of Petroleum Resources. Those discussions were constuctive,&quot; said a spokesman for Ashland.</p>
<p>&quot;We are currently in discussions with Total, but those discussions are confidential and have not concluded,&quot; the spokesman added.</p>
<p>The Nigerian government said in June that it had withdrawn four licenses because Ashland Oil Co, a unit of Ashland, had sold its interest without the written consent of the government.</p>
<p>Ashland had been in talks with privately-held Perenco Investments of France over the assets when the licenses were cancelled.</p>
<p>((-- David Chance New York Newsroom 212 859 1902))</p>
